 "light": "Dawn from the east (about 5 degrees); evening and dusk sun from about 195 degrees over the house roof; the gate lamp at every dark; the evening wind from the west.",
 "notes": [
  "The farm stands on a terrace on the valley's north side: from west to east the house, the yard with the fold in it, and the one gate in the yard's east wall, facing down the road.",
  "The yard is 34 m east to west and 30 m north to south inside a dry-stone wall 0.7 m thick and about 1.7 m high (a man's shoulder and one course more); the house stands in its west wall.",
  "The gate is a 2.7 m opening between two fieldstone posts 0.9 m square under a timber lintel; its one olive-wood leaf hangs on the south post and stands open into the yard; the gate is never barred.",
  "The lamp niche (origin) is a small arch cut through the north gatepost at shoulder height, so its flame shows down the road and across the yard; it can be lit from either side.",
  "The house is the owner's one room (eliab_house), 5.25 by 3.0 m inside; its doorway is in the east wall 34 m west of the gate on the gateway's axis (y = -1.8), so from the gateway you see into the lit room and from the table you see the gate lamp.",
  "The stone bench runs 2.4 m along the outer foot of the wall just north of the north post; the trough stands outside just south of the south post.",
  "The fold (14 by 10 m, chest-high walls, room for the hundred) is on the yard's north side with its barred gate facing south onto the lane from the gate to the house door; the ox byre and the calf pen with its rail are east of it.",
  "The ovens are in the yard south-east of the house; the hand mill is inside the house by its LEFT wall; the cistern is in the yard near the gate.",
  "The threshing floor (9 m across, edged with set stones) is outside the yard on the terrace's south edge, about 2 m lower than the gate and open to the evening wind; the floor track climbs from it to the road just below the gate, and the footpath from the village climbs to it through a gap in the terrace wall.",
  "The hill track leaves the road 9 m east of the gate and climbs north-east to the hill pasture; the road goes east, then bends south-east down to the village gate about 500 m away (eliab_valley).",
  "The eaves overhang the house's east wall by about 1 m; Asher's night mat lies under them just north of the doorway (Sc 2).",
  "Dawn comes from the east over the valley (about 5 degrees); the evening and dusk sun comes from about 195 degrees over the house roof; the evening wind blows from the west, down the valley, so chaff goes east and downhill."
 ],
